# Accessibility

Every new interactive feature should consider:

- screen reader labels
- touch target size
- text scaling
- contrast
- focus order
- keyboard navigation where relevant
- reduced motion
- error announcements where supported

Icon-only controls require an accessible label.

Do not use emojis as the only semantic indicator.

Forms must expose validation errors in a way assistive technologies can understand.

Do not disable accessibility to make a design look cleaner.
